{"title":"Lisa Rosenthal, Ph.D.","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Lisa Rosenthal, Ph.D.","image":"profile_pic.jpg","about":{"template":"trestles","links":[{"icon":"linkedin","text":"LinkedIn","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lisamr/"},{"icon":"github","text":"github","href":"https://github.com/lisamr"}]}},"headingText":"About me","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n:::{#hero-heading}\n\n\nI'm a forest and fire ecologist with a heavy data science slant. \n\nAs an applied Bayesian statistics nerd, I'm making the leap into the world of machine learning. With an interest in applying remote sensing data to monitor forest and fire activity and measure fuels with better accuracy, I'm dedicating time to learning the ins and outs of ML. \n\nI'm following the [fast.ai course](https://course.fast.ai/) and I will be blogging about what I am learning and applying to real data. Check out my blog posts and follow along! \n\n## Education\n\nPhD in Ecology<br>\nUniversity of California, Davis<br>\n2016 - 2021\n\nBS in Molecular Env. Biology<br>\nUniversity of California, Berkeley<br>\n2009 - 2013\n\n## Experience\n\nCalifornia Air Resources Board | Wildfire Emissions Inventory Specialist | Sept 2023 - present\n\nU.S. Geological Survey | Wildland Fuels Researcher | Sept 2021 - Aug 2023\n\nUC Davis | National Science Foundation Graduate Research Fellow | 2016 - 2021 ","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n:::{#hero-heading}\n\n## About me\n\nI'm a forest and fire ecologist with a heavy data science slant. \n\nAs an applied Bayesian statistics nerd, I'm making the leap into the world of machine learning. With an interest in applying remote sensing data to monitor forest and fire activity and measure fuels with better accuracy, I'm dedicating time to learning the ins and outs of ML. \n\nI'm following the [fast.ai course](https://course.fast.ai/) and I will be blogging about what I am learning and applying to real data. Check out my blog posts and follow along! \n\n## Education\n\nPhD in Ecology<br>\